extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 48-49. The Experience Tables on printed 214 call this
    class "Sea Inquisitioner"; the chapter heading on printed 48 calls it the
    "Sea Inquisitor O.C.C.". The heading spelling is stored because it is the
    one the entry itself uses throughout, and the ladder spelling is recorded
    here. This is the one place in this book where the stored name follows the
    heading rather than the authority table, and the reason is that the ladder
    entry looks like a typo of the heading rather than a different name.
  - ITS RELATED AND SECONDARY SKILLS ARE ANOTHER CLASS''S AND ARE NOT STORED.
    This is BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F23(a), which is OPEN - printed 49 has the
    player draw them from any Scholar or Adventurer O.C.C., any Psychic
    R.C.C., or from the sailor, pirate, grunt/foot-soldier, simple warrior or
    mystic. There is no key for "use that class''s list". Added to F23(a)''s
    affected rows rather than filed as a new finding, per the batch rule.
    THE CLASS THEREFORE GRANTS SIX SKILLS AND NOTHING ELSE, and a character
    built from it will look thin until a second list is picked by hand. That is
    the book''s shape, not a dropped count: printed 49 names the source lists
    and gives no number at all.
  - "+1 TO SAVE VS ALL MAGIC" IS WRITTEN OUT AS SIX KEYS. The sheet draws
    sixteen saves from a literal list, so a blanket bonus has to be stated
    against each one to appear. `spell_magic`, `ritual_magic`,
    `illusionary_magic`, `faerie_magic`, `curses` and `mind_control` are the
    six that are magic; `mind_control` is included because printed 49 names it
    explicitly. The book also names potions, circles and wards, and the sheet
    has no save row for any of the three.
  - NO PSIONICS BLOCK, DELIBERATELY. Printed 49 gives a distribution rather
    than a grant - about 45% of sea inquisitors have no psychic ability at all,
    50% minor or major, 5% master or magic - so the class grants none and the
    distribution is a restriction line. Storing a psionics block would hand
    every sea inquisitor powers that 45% of them do not have.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so this class needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS`
    entry in `js/compose.js` or the smoke test fails it. Set to 1D6 rather than
    3D6: Underseas does not sort its O.C.C.s into Palladium''s men-of-arms and
    scholar sections, so there is no heading to read it off, and the class''s own
    combat training is Hand to Hand: Basic and two W.P.s - not a man of arms.
    The +2D6x10 S.D.C. the class grants is a POOL bonus on top of that, which is
    what the book means by "+2D6x10 S.D.C.".
  - THE DISPERSAL ABILITY IS PROSE AND CANNOT BE OTHERWISE. Ten points of
    P.P.E./I.S.P. cancellation per level per melee round, spent across however
    many incoming attacks it covers, with a half-effect tier when it falls
    short, is a resource the app has no shape for. It is a `special_abilities`
    entry with the full rule in it.
  - THE DOUBLE-DAMAGE ABILITY IS ALSO PROSE. A conditional damage multiplier
    against a creature type is not something `bonuses.combat` can express -
    `damage_bonus` is a flat addend - so it is a special ability.
