# Sea Inquisitor

## Lore

Humans who have heard the calling of the Lord of the Deep and kept their sanity enough to refuse it often become obsessed with destroying the monster and everything it has made. So do sailors and adventurers who have simply seen the thing in all its horror. Their brush with the supernatural wakes something in them, and they use it to hunt down the cults and creations of the alien intelligence.

They are called Witch Finders or Inquisitors, and because they work the seacoasts and islands and travel the seas where cultists and minions are found, they are usually called Sea Inquisitors.

Most led ordinary lives until that encounter. Those with psionics were touched in dreams and visions and offered great power in exchange for their humanity; those with strong wills, good alignment or high principles refused, and paid for it in splitting headaches and a temporary insanity lasting 2D6 days after the last dream. When they recovered, they were changed - and knowing they could fight the horror in their own minds, they understood they could fight it in the world.

## GM Notes

Sea inquisitors work alone or in small groups. They have no global organisation and no central base, and yet they all have similar powers and similar goals. Some speculate they are empowered by a Higher Force opposed to the Lord of the Deep. But there is not a flicker of supernatural energy around them despite their mystical powers, which leaves open whether the source is an essence too subtle to detect or simply their own conviction. Nobody knows.

They become experienced witch and demon hunters, fighting not only the servants of the Lord of the Deep but every other foul and inhuman creature they meet, in a standing quest to destroy supernatural evil wherever it is. They often join forces with whale singers, undead slayers, cyber-knights, adventurers and other champions of good.
', 'published', 'data-script'
